# A raw read of a loader global: Kani checks the read on a live, aligned
# `T` holding any value at both instances `probe` uses; that the address
# `symbols` returns is such a `T` is the loader's (L1). The pin keeps
# `probe` the only caller, with `probe`'s and `area`'s code line for line,
# `symbols`' signature, `Probe`'s field types and `CPU_ID_OFFSET`; 13 source
# mutants of those (a new caller, a turbofish, a rename, a fn pointer, a
# dropped null check, a moved offset, a shadowing `let`, ...) each fail it.
# Its known escapes: a call spelled from parts by a macro (`paste!`,
# `concat_idents!`), and code `include!`d from outside `src/`.
read_global	raw pointer (internal)	Kani	discharged on premises (Kani: rseq::kani_rseq::read_global_reads_the_value; premises: L1 (a non-null address `symbols` returns is glibc's live, aligned `isize` or `u32`, which nothing writes after startup, in a dynamic link; `probe` passes those three at the two instances the harness runs; and the provenance of an `asm!` output, premises.md: Provenance of the addresses); callers: rseq::tests::probe_reads_are_listed)	contract 1325462615, body 4072880412, spec 3955195640
# A volatile read of the kernel-written `cpu_id`: Kani checks the read on
# an area the `requires` admits; that `area` is this thread's rseq area is
# glibc's and the rseq ABI's (L1, L2). The same pin, mutants and escapes
# as `read_global`'s keep `probe` the only caller, on `area` of the offset.
read_cpu_id	UnsafeCell/volatile/transmute	Kani	discharged on premises (Kani: rseq::kani_rseq::read_cpu_id_reads_the_field; premises: L1 (`__rseq_offset` is stored before challoc runs and never after) and L2 (in a thread glibc created, the thread pointer plus `__rseq_offset` is its rseq area, at least 32 bytes and 32-byte aligned, whose `cpu_id` only glibc and the kernel write, never during the thread's own load; `probe` passes `area` of that offset; and the provenance of an exposed address, premises.md: Provenance of the addresses); callers: rseq::tests::probe_reads_are_listed)	contract 1095263007, body 1368553990
# Inline assembly checked with Isla (verus/ISLA.md): run.sh checks
# each against the contract verus/isla/seams.md quotes.
symbols	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	discharged (Isla: verus/isla/seams.md)	contract 1031842438, body 2186581197
thread_pointer	inline asm	Islaris/Isla	discharged (Isla: verus/isla/seams.md)	contract 542526640, body 2144560029
